Third-party source code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository carries the public IW4L and 2010 Rust Rewrite Mashup sources.
Its Cargo dependencies remain under their respective licences. It also carries
the following public engine sources in-tree as inherited from that mashup. The
project's Apache-2.0 licence applies to its own code only; it does not relicense
the inherited material below:

skate/ — engine crates from SK8-ENGINE/skate-3-rust-engine, revision cb79689,
  and the inherited skating integration/data converter.
  https://github.com/SK8-ENGINE/skate-3-rust-engine
  The upstream project describes its code as based on Skate 3 reverse-
  engineering research and states that its original code is GPL-3.0-only.
  Preserve that licence for this inherited tree; the top-level Apache-2.0
  declaration does not relicense it. Some inherited comments/constants refer
  to Xbox 360 TU3 executable addresses and values learned from the executable.
  The legacy converter reads an external Skate 3 installation. No proprietary
  Skate 3 executable, model, texture, animation or sound data is bundled.

third_party/minecraftoss/ — five crates of MinecraftOSS, a Rust Minecraft
  engine, copied from its commit 4013a68 (see its README). Its few data
  tables are gameplay values measured from Minecraft (food, waxing and
  dispenser rules). No Minecraft code, JARs, textures or sounds are included:
  the inherited optional Minecraft mode downloads Minecraft's files from
  Mojang on first run. It is not the standalone survival game's content path.
  The vendored snapshot contains no licence file or licence declaration. Its
  licence has not been independently established; do not treat it as
  Apache-2.0 or redistribute it as release content until MinecraftOSS confirms
  the applicable licence.

mods/rust/client/generator/interop/pointer-byref.patch — a two-predicate
  correction to BepInEx/Il2CppInterop, source revision
  dbda1cb353b0f4253345dc45136d170b9e50a5a0.
  https://github.com/BepInEx/Il2CppInterop
  The modified library source remains LGPL-3.0-only; full LGPL/GPL texts and
  modification attribution are in that directory's UPSTREAM-LICENSE and
  MODIFICATIONS-LICENSE. The separate project-authored recipe/configuration
  remains Apache-2.0. The recipe stages the original upstream source archive,
  exact patch and build inputs alongside its Generator candidate; no upstream
  DLL, generated client assembly or proprietary game file is committed here.

mods/rust/shared/SkateAudio.cs — original project-authored procedural audio.
  Wheel, truck/deck-contact and event PCM is generated from seeded oscillators,
  filtered noise and damped resonators. No sampled game audio, commercial sample
  library, synthesizer preset or third-party sound asset is distributed. This
  source and its generated original waveforms use the project's Apache-2.0 licence.

Bundled inherited/generated data with open provenance:

crates/fx_iw4/data/fx_random_table.bin
  This is byte-for-byte identical to the file in upstream IW4L and was
  inherited from there. Neither repository currently records whether it was
  authored, generated from public research, or copied from a game. Its origin
  and redistribution permission remain to be confirmed with the IW4L author.

crates/assets/data/minecraft/*-26.3.json.gz
  These four compressed catalogs are exported by MinecraftOSS's harness for
  the pinned Minecraft 26.3 data. They are not the Mojang client JAR or asset
  objects. The launcher separately downloads Mojang's 26.3 files on first run.
  Their exact licence and redistribution permission follow the unresolved
  MinecraftOSS provenance above.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
References consulted during development
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ReSkate — https://github.com/Dingo-Shenanigans/ReSkate
  ReSkate contributors' GPL-3.0-licensed extension for the existing skate. game.
  Consulted for park-editing lifecycle, controller input and runtime compatibility
  patterns while designing the existing-Rust skate mod. No ReSkate source,
  native integration data or game assets are copied, linked or bundled here.

REA (Reverse Engineer Anything) — https://github.com/morluto/rea
  morluto and contributors' MIT-licensed reverse-engineering toolkit.
  Consulted for static managed-code inspection capabilities and evidence limits.
  No REA source, package, binaries or analysis output are bundled here.

Facepunch Rust.World — https://github.com/Facepunch/Rust.World
  Public MIT-licensed world editor SDK. Its version-9 protobuf declarations,
  serialized map envelope and terrain conversion informed rust_maps. The
  SDK source and original Rust assets are not bundled.

LZ4.NET — https://github.com/MiloszKrajewski/lz4net
  Public legacy LZ4Stream envelope specification studied for version-9 maps.
  The C# implementation is not copied or linked; block decompression uses
  the independently declared lz4_flex Cargo dependency.

These projects were read while working out how the original games behave. They
are named here because the reading happened, not because anything of theirs is
distributed: none of them is vendored, linked, bundled or otherwise shipped.

OpenAssetTools — https://github.com/Laupetin/OpenAssetTools
  Open-source modding tools for older Call of Duty games. Its asset-structure
  headers document the on-disk layouts IW4L reads. Licensed under GPLv3.

oat (iw4x-x64 fork of OpenAssetTools) — https://github.com/iw4x-x64/oat
  The x64 fork, at revision 3a7442dee5ce040cfdb8da23fdb9fb525b5f743e, is the
  tree whose IW4MS headers were read for the 64-bit FastFile layouts.
  Licensed under GPLv3, like its upstream. No file in this repository is
  compiled against, generated from or distributed with those headers.

IW4x — https://github.com/iw4x/iw4x-client
  A custom client for Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2 (2009), with dedicated
  servers, security fixes and modding support. Read as a cross-reference for
  asset and protocol behaviour, and by the fork for controller aim assist. Licensed under GPLv3.

KisakCOD — https://github.com/SwagSoftware/KisakCOD
  A Call of Duty 4 open-source reimplementation. Read as a cross-reference for
  engine structure, and by the fork for controller aim assist's defaults. IW4L targets IW4, so this is a neighbouring generation of
  the same engine family, not the same codebase.

Unity C# reference source — https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/UnityCsReference
  Read to check the Unity 6 object-marshalling and read-only physics API contract
  used by the optional Rust client collision observations. Reference only;
  no Unity reference-source implementation is copied or distributed here.
  Unity Reference-Only License.

Ghidra — https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra
  The software reverse engineering framework the original game binaries were
  read with. A development tool: none of it, and none of its output, is
  committed here or distributed with IW4L. Licensed under Apache 2.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Game content
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The standalone PC game is being built with newly authored content and public
engine code, inspired by survival, military FPS and skateboard games. Its
default launcher path uses assets/authored and requires no original game
installation. Optional inherited modes differ: IW4L/MW2 import reads a user's
MW2 install; the Skate converter reads an extracted Skate 3 Xbox 360
default.xex with its data folder; the Minecraft mode downloads Minecraft 26.3
files from Mojang and uses the inherited MinecraftOSS catalogs. Procedural
building materials are authored in this repository's WGSL renderer.

No proprietary Call of Duty, Rust, Skate or Minecraft game assets are bundled.
The inherited optional IW4L import modes can read an external game installation;
their presence does not mean those files are included or needed by the planned
standalone content path.

